# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/maps/tide_caves.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event docks_sea_back_door
# en: The Sea's Back Door
title [af7b40] = 海的后门
# en: An old docker on the breakwater sees you looking at the headland and takes his pipe out. "The sea's back door," he says. "Under there. Open at low water, noon and after, and shut the rest. Smugglers' road in my grandad's time. Still is, some say." The pipe goes back in. "The sea lets you in easy. It's coming out that wants thinking about."
text [23df42] = 防波堤上一个老码头工看见你在望那片岬角，便把烟斗从嘴里拿了出来。“海的后门，”他说，“就在那底下。退潮时开，正午和午后，别的时候关着。我爷爷那会儿是走私的道。有人说现在还是。”烟斗又塞回嘴里。“海放你进去容易。出来才要好好想想。”
# en: An old docker with a clay pipe at the end of a stone breakwater, pointing across the water to a rocky headland with a dark cave mouth at its foot, a student beside him.
scene [4ed5d3] = 石砌防波堤尽头，一个叼着陶土烟斗的老码头工指着水对面一片岩石岬角，岬角脚下有个黑洞洞的洞口，一个学生站在他身旁。
# en: Buy him a pint for the way
opt.left.label [4568a0] = 请他喝一杯，问问路
# en: You stand him a pint, and he walks you out to the end of the breakwater and points the way with his pipe stem: along the rocks, past a white mark painted high on one, down the steps. "Out by the time the water's at the mark," he says. "Not after."
opt.left.say.1 [601b7c] = 你请他喝了一品脱，他领你走到防波堤尽头，用烟斗杆给你指路：沿着礁石走，经过一块高处刷了白记号的石头，再顺着台阶下去。“水涨到记号之前出来，”他说，“别等之后。”
# en: Go and find it yourself
opt.right.label [93338f] = 自己去找
# en: You scramble off the end of the breakwater and over the weedy rocks beyond, slip twice, bark a shin, and find it: a dark mouth under the headland, with cold air coming out of it like a cellar's.
opt.right.say.1 [05ba05] = 你从防波堤尽头爬下去，翻过满是海草的礁石，滑了两跤，磕破了小腿，终于找到了：岬角底下一个黑洞，冷气从里面往外冒，像地窖口一样。

@event tide_rock_pools
# en: The Rock Pools
title [4b8152] = 礁石潭
# en: {&At low water the headland shows its feet: black rock, weed like wet hair, and rock pools full of anemones that shut when your shadow falls on them. Behind them the cave mouth is a black slot in the rock.|The rock pools again. A shrimp the colour of glass, a crab backing into a crack, a hermit crab trying on a new shell. The tide's still going out.|The pools are clear as glass today. A small boy with a jam-jar is working the far ones, very seriously, and tells you not to touch his.}
text [25b64e] = {&退潮时岬角露出了脚：黑色的礁石，湿头发似的海草，还有一个个礁石潭，里面的海葵在你的影子落上去时就合拢了。它们后面，洞口是岩石上一道黑缝。|又是这些礁石潭。一只玻璃色的小虾，一只倒退着钻进石缝的螃蟹，一只寄居蟹在试一个新壳。潮水还在往外退。|今天潭水清得像玻璃。一个拿着果酱罐的小男孩正一本正经地搜着远处那几个潭，还叫你别碰他的。}
# en: Rock pools on a wet rocky shore under a headland at low tide, anemones and weed, a student crouching over a pool, a small boy with a jam-jar further off, a dark cave mouth behind.
scene [418973] = 退潮时岬角下湿漉漉的礁石岸，礁石潭里有海葵和海草，一个学生蹲在潭边，远处一个拿果酱罐的小男孩，后面是一个黑洞口。
# en: Poke about the pools
opt.left.label [8a2d81] = 在潭里翻翻找找
# en: {&You learn the anemones by poking them, which they don't like, and the barnacles by kneeling on them, which you don't. Your knees bleed a little.|You lift weed and watch the pools empty of everything, fast. A crab gets your thumb and keeps it a while.|You and the boy compare jars. His is better. You cut your knee on the rock, kneeling to admit it.}
opt.left.say.1 [3a94e9] = {&你靠戳海葵认识了海葵，它们不乐意；靠跪在藤壶上认识了藤壶，你不乐意。膝盖渗了点血。|你掀起海草，看着潭里的东西一眨眼全跑光了。一只螃蟹夹住你的拇指，夹了好一会儿。|你和那男孩比罐子。他的更好。你跪在礁石上认输时划破了膝盖。}
# en: Pick mussels for supper
opt.right.label [865800] = 采些贻贝当晚饭
# en: {&You fill your hat with mussels off the rocks and soak both sleeves to the shoulder in cold water. Cooked on the quay with an onion, they're the best thing you've eaten in the capital.|You pick mussels with numb fingers while the sea comes back, and get your boots full running from it. Supper's good. Your feet aren't.|You pick a hatful. The boy says the ones by the outfall make you ill. You throw half back, sulking, and eat the rest.}
opt.right.say.1 [9eb534] = {&你从礁石上采了满满一帽子贻贝，两只袖子一直湿到肩膀，冰凉。在码头上配个洋葱一煮，是你在王都吃过最好的东西。|你用冻僵的手指采贻贝，潮水回来了，你跑开时灌了一靴子水。晚饭不错。脚不太好。|你采了一帽子。男孩说排水口那边的吃了会生病。你闷闷不乐地扔回去一半，把剩下的吃了。}

@event tide_bait_diggers
# en: The Bait-Diggers
title [ae6d6a] = 挖饵人
# en: {&Bait-diggers are out on the sand below the headland, turning it over with forks for lugworm. An old woman among them keeps glancing up at a white mark painted high on a rock. When the sea touches that, she says, you want to be on the sand, not under the headland.|The bait-diggers again, and the old woman watching her white mark. "Going in, are you?" she asks. "You'll have heard what they say on the docks. Out by the mark."|The diggers are resting on their buckets. The old woman offers you a fork and a bucket, then her flask, in that order.}
text [a56b54] = {&挖饵人在岬角下的沙滩上，用叉子翻沙挖沙蚕。其中一个老妇人不时抬头看一块礁石高处刷的白记号。她说，海水一碰到那里，你最好是在沙滩上，而不是在岬角底下。|又是挖饵人，那个老妇人还盯着她的白记号。“要进去，是吧？”她问，“码头上那句话你听说过吧。到记号就出来。”|挖饵人们靠着桶歇息。老妇人递给你一把叉子、一只桶，然后是她的酒壶，就按这个顺序。}
# en: Men and women with forks and buckets digging for worms on wet sand under a rocky headland at low tide, an old woman pointing up at a white mark painted on a rock, a student watching.
scene [06da97] = 退潮时岩石岬角下的湿沙滩上，男男女女拿着叉子和桶挖虫子，一个老妇人指着礁石上刷的白记号，一个学生在一旁看着。
# en: Dig bait with them
opt.left.label [f9b7f3] = 跟他们一起挖饵
# en: {&You dig till your back's a knot and sell your bucket of worms to an angler on the breakwater for a few coins. The old woman says you dig like a gentleman, which isn't praise.|An hour of forking wet sand. The bucket fetches a few coins on the breakwater; your back will fetch you nothing but trouble tomorrow.|You dig with them till the sea turns, and come away with coins in your pocket, sand where sand shouldn't go and a back like a plank.}
opt.left.say.1 [4ca957] = {&你挖到腰都拧成了疙瘩，把一桶虫子卖给防波堤上的钓鱼人，换了几枚硬币。老妇人说你挖起来像个绅士，这可不是夸你。|叉了一个钟头湿沙。那桶虫在防波堤上换了几枚硬币；你的腰明天只会给你换来麻烦。|你跟他们一直挖到潮水回头，兜里揣着硬币，沙子进了不该进的地方，腰硬得像块木板。}
# en: Ask about the caves
opt.right.label [6baa0e] = 打听那些洞
# en: {&"Free traders," she says. "My mother's brothers ran brandy through there under the customs men's feet. Some still do. The sea takes its share." She won't say more, and you feel uneasy all afternoon.|"There's a door at the far end," she says, "on the sea side. You'll know it." She looks at you as if you're already wet.|"The ones that don't come out," she says, "the sea gives back at the breakwater, after." Then she offers you the flask again. You don't want it now.}
opt.right.say.1 [b44ebe] = {&“私货贩子，”她说，“我娘家的兄弟们就在海关的人脚底下从那里运白兰地。现在也还有人干。海要拿它那一份。”她不肯再多说，你整个下午都心里发毛。|“最里头有扇门，”她说，“在海那一边。你见了就知道。”她看你的样子，好像你已经湿透了。|“那些没出来的，”她说，“海过后会在防波堤那儿还回来。”然后她又把酒壶递给你。你现在不想要了。}

@event tide_cave_mouth
# en: The Cave Mouth
title [268672] = 洞口
# en: {tide_deepest == 0: Under the headland the cave mouth stands open at low water, tall as a church door, breathing out cold and the smell of weed. Steps cut in the rock lead down into it, worn hollow by feet that went down a long time ago. The sea's a long way out. It's coming back.|{&The cave mouth, and the steps going down, and the cold breath out of it.|The cave mouth at low water. Somewhere far inside, the sea is talking to itself.|The cave mouth. The white mark on the rock is dry, for now.}} {flag(tide_calder_run): You know which gallery the smugglers' run takes.|}
text [a078ea] = {tide_deepest == 0: 岬角底下，洞口在退潮时敞开着，高得像教堂的门，往外呼着寒气和海草味。岩石上凿出的台阶通下去，被很久以前走下去的脚磨出了凹痕。海退得很远。它会回来的。|{&洞口，往下去的台阶，从里面吐出来的冷气。|退潮时的洞口。深处某个地方，海在自言自语。|洞口。礁石上的白记号还是干的，暂时。}} {flag(tide_calder_run): 你知道走私者的路走哪条坑道。|}
# en: A tall dark cave mouth at the foot of a rocky headland at low tide, wet steps cut in the rock going down into it, a student with a lantern at the entrance, the harbour behind.
scene [e9486b] = 退潮时岩石岬角脚下一个高高的黑洞口，岩石上凿出的湿台阶通向洞里，一个提着灯的学生站在洞口，身后是港口。
# en: Stay out on the rocks
opt.left.label [d0dafc] = 待在外面的礁石上
# en: {&You stay out on the rocks in the sun and let the cave keep its cold.|Not today. You watch the sea come back from the dry side of it.|You stay out. The cave breathes at you, and you breathe back, from a distance.}
opt.left.say.1 [449126] = {&你待在外面晒太阳的礁石上，让洞自己留着它的冷。|今天不了。你在干的那一边看着海回来。|你待在外面。洞朝你呼气，你也朝它呼气，隔着一段距离。}
# en: Go down the steps
opt.right.label [26f409] = 走下台阶
# en: A delve: press on card by card, turn back any time.
opt.right.hint [e6594e] = 探洞：一张张往前走，随时可以回头。
# en: {flag(tide_calder_run): You take the smugglers' run, straight past the easy caves, reading the tide ladder's hooks as you go.|{has(origin_street) and tide_deepest == 0: You went in here once at eleven, on a dare from the crew, and came out at a run. You go in at a walk this time.|You go down the steps into the cold. Behind you the daylight gets small and square.}}
opt.right.say.1 [428ee1] = {flag(tide_calder_run): 你走走私者的路，径直越过那些好走的洞，一路读着潮梯上的钩记。|{has(origin_street) and tide_deepest == 0: 你十一岁那年被伙伴们激着进来过一次，是跑着出去的。这次你是走着进去的。|你顺着台阶走进寒气里。身后的天光变得又小又方。}}

@event tide_way_out
# en: Back in the Daylight
title [3699ac] = 回到天光下
# en: {tide_swam == 1: You stand dripping on the breakwater among the anglers, with what the sea let you keep. They want to see it.|{tide_haul == 0: You come up out of the caves with nothing but wet boots and the sea's voice in your ears.|{tide_haul <= 2: You come up into the daylight with a light, dripping bag: a copper nail, sea-glass, an old coin gone green.|{tide_haul <= 4: You come up with a bag that clinks: old coin, a brass fitting, bottles with something still in them.|You come up bent under a heavy, dripping sack, and the sea comes in behind you as if it had been waiting.}}}} {tide_depth >= 5: Salt has dried white on your sleeves.|}
text [f511ad] = {tide_swam == 1: 你湿淋淋地站在防波堤上的钓鱼人中间，手里是海肯让你留下的东西。他们想看看。|{tide_haul == 0: 你从洞里出来，除了一双湿靴子和耳朵里海的声音，什么也没有。|{tide_haul <= 2: 你回到天光下，提着一只轻飘飘、滴着水的袋子：一根铜钉，几块海玻璃，一枚生了绿锈的旧硬币。|{tide_haul <= 4: 你出来时袋子叮当作响：旧硬币，一个黄铜配件，几个里面还有东西的瓶子。|你背着一只沉甸甸、滴着水的大袋子弯腰出来，海在你身后涌进来，好像一直在等着。}}}} {tide_depth >= 5: 你的袖子上结了一层白盐。|}
# en: A tired, wet student climbing out of a sea cave into daylight on a rocky shore, a dripping sack over one shoulder, a quay and a cluttered junk shop behind.
scene [048efa] = 一个疲惫、湿透的学生从海蚀洞爬出来，走到礁石岸上的天光里，肩上搭着滴水的袋子，身后是码头和一家杂乱的旧货铺。
# en: Sell it on the quay
opt.left.label [9685e4] = 在码头上卖掉
# en: Crowns, by what you carry.
opt.left.hint [0ece3c] = 克朗，看你带出来多少。
# en: {tide_haul == 0: The marine-store dealer on the quay looks at your empty hands and laughs until he coughs.|{&The marine-store dealer on the quay weighs it all on a scale meant for anchors and pays by the pound, asking nothing, which is how Port Calder likes it.|The dealer tips your bag out on his counter, sorts it with one finger, and pays. "Further in," he says, "it's worth more. So I hear."|The dealer pays without looking up. Half his shop, you realise, came out of those caves.}}
opt.left.say.1 [e30cf3] = {tide_haul == 0: 码头上的船具旧货商看看你空空的手，笑到咳嗽。|{&码头上的船具旧货商把东西全放在一杆称锚用的秤上，按斤给钱，什么也不问，考尔德港就喜欢这样。|旧货商把你的袋子倒在柜台上，用一根手指拨了拨，付了钱。“再往里，”他说，“东西更值钱。我听说的。”|旧货商头也不抬就付了钱。你这才意识到，他铺子里一半的东西都是从那些洞里出来的。}}
# en: Keep it for study
opt.right.label [2aa44b] = 留着研究
# en: Alchemy and lore, by what you carry.
opt.right.hint [52aee6] = 炼金和学识，看你带出来多少。
# en: {tide_haul == 0: You keep nothing but the cold, and a better idea of the caves.|{&You lay it all out on a table: salt crusted on everything, sea-glass, a phial of something that was a cure for something once. You spend the night working out what.|You scrape the salt off every piece and keep it in a jar. It's purer than anything in the bazaar.|You sort it all by lamplight. One old coin has a ship on one side and nothing at all on the other.}}
opt.right.say.1 [f6a19a] = {tide_haul == 0: 你什么也没留下，只有寒意，还有对那些洞多了几分了解。|{&你把东西全摊在桌上：每样都结着盐，海玻璃，一小瓶曾经能治什么病的东西。你花了一整夜弄清楚是什么病。|你把每件东西上的盐都刮下来，装进一个罐子。比集市上任何东西都纯。|你就着灯光一件件分类。有一枚旧硬币，一面是条船，另一面什么也没有。}}

@event tide_soaked
# en: Soaked to the Skin
title [5bb8c1] = 湿透了
# en: {tide_dropped == 1: {&A wave you never saw slaps you off the ledge into the swirl, and something rolls out of your bag and is gone.|You come up coughing on a ledge with a cut hand and a lighter bag. The sea's still sucking at your boots.|The rock is weed and the weed is glass. You go down, and the pool keeps a little of what you carried.}|{&A wave you never saw slaps you off the ledge into the swirl, and you come up with a mouthful of the sea and an empty bag that had nothing to lose.|You come up coughing on a ledge with a cut hand. The sea's still sucking at your boots.|The rock is weed and the weed is glass. You go down hard, and come up bruised and soaked to the collar.}} {tide_grace > 0: You've got one more ducking in you, maybe.|That was your last easy fall.}
text [8e526f] = {tide_dropped == 1: {&一个你根本没看见的浪把你从岩架上拍进了漩涡，袋子里滚出去一样东西，没了。|你在一块岩架上咳着冒出头来，手划破了，袋子也轻了。海还在吸你的靴子。|石头上是海草，海草滑得像玻璃。你摔了下去，水潭留下了你带着的一点东西。}|{&一个你根本没看见的浪把你从岩架上拍进了漩涡，你冒出头来，灌了一嘴海水，好在袋子是空的，也没什么可丢。|你在一块岩架上咳着冒出头来，手划破了。海还在吸你的靴子。|石头上是海草，海草滑得像玻璃。你重重摔了下去，爬起来时一身青紫，湿到了领口。}} {tide_grace > 0: 你大概还经得起一次落水。|那是你最后一次摔得不重。}
# en: A student sitting soaked on a wet rock ledge in a dim sea cave, coughing, a spilled bag beside them, sea water swirling below.
scene [cc2cb8] = 昏暗的海蚀洞里，一个学生湿透了坐在湿岩架上咳嗽，身边洒了一地的袋子，下面海水打着旋。
# en: That's enough for today
opt.left.label [3d2940] = 今天就到这儿
# en: {&You wring yourself out and feel your way back toward the light.|You've had enough of the sea, and the sea of you, for now.|You turn back, following the drip of fresh water toward the light.}
opt.left.say.1 [69581d] = {&你把自己拧干，摸索着往有光的地方回去。|你受够了海，海也受够了你，暂时。|你往回走，顺着淡水滴落的方向朝光那边去。}
# en: Get up and go on
opt.right.label [813dfe] = 爬起来继续走
# en: Deeper: the next fall may not be kind.
opt.right.hint [cae0c4] = 更深处：下一次摔倒未必这么客气。
# en: {&You wring out your sleeves and go on, squelching.|You get up. The sea draws back from the ledge as if nothing had happened.|You go on. Behind you, the water has covered the step you came by.}
opt.right.say.1 [29a2f6] = {&你拧干袖子，咕叽咕叽地继续往前走。|你爬起来。海从岩架上退开，好像什么也没发生过。|你继续往前。身后，水已经淹没了你来时踩的那级台阶。}

@event tide_fished_out
# en: Fished Out
title [04e10a] = 被捞上来
# en: {at_home() and has(origin_street): The tide comes in faster than you can go out. You end up on a ledge in the dark with the water at your chin, until a rope comes down out of nowhere, and at the top of it is Nan Merrow, swearing.|The tide comes in faster than you can go out. You spend hours on a ledge with the sea at your chest, until it turns and lets you crawl for the mouth, and a lighterman out after driftwood hauls you into his boat with a boathook.} {tide_bag_lost == 1: Your bag, and everything you salvaged in it, went with the flood, somewhere in the dark of the caves.|}
text [08b38d] = {at_home() and has(origin_street): 潮水涨得比你出去得快。你困在黑暗里的一块岩架上，水淹到下巴，直到一根绳子不知从哪里垂下来，绳子那头是南·梅罗，正骂骂咧咧。|潮水涨得比你出去得快。你在一块岩架上待了好几个钟头，海水淹到胸口，直到潮水回头，你才爬向洞口，一个出来捞漂木的驳船夫用船钩把你拖进了他的船。} {tide_bag_lost == 1: 你的袋子，连同你捞上来的所有东西，都被涨潮卷走了，不知沉在洞里哪片黑暗中。|}
# en: A rocky shore under a headland in grey evening light, a man in a small rowing boat hauling a half-drowned, shivering student out of the water with a boathook.
scene [f8aef2] = 灰暗的傍晚光线里岬角下的礁石岸，一个坐在小划艇里的男人用船钩把一个半淹、发抖的学生从水里拖上来。
# en: Thank them and go quietly
opt.left.label [10e7a7] = 道个谢，安静地走
# en: {at_home() and has(origin_street): She walks you back to the loft by the scruff and sits you by the stove in the crew's worst blanket. "Through the caves," she tells the room, "on the flood," and the whole loft groans.|He rows you to the harbour steps and won't take a coin. "On the flood," he says, shaking his head. "They always go in on the ebb and think it'll last."}
opt.left.say.1 [4eadec] = {at_home() and has(origin_street): 她揪着你的后领把你押回阁楼，把你按在炉子边，裹上伙伴们最破的毯子。“钻洞，”她对满屋子人说，“赶上涨潮，”整个阁楼一片哀叹。|他把你划到港口台阶边，一个硬币也不收。“赶上涨潮，”他摇着头说，“他们总是退潮时进去，以为能一直退下去。”}
# en: Ask how they knew to look
opt.right.label [91390b] = 问他们怎么知道来找
# en: {at_home() and has(origin_street): "The gulls went in," she says. "They only go in after something that's drowning." She says it as flat as a price.|"Gulls," he says. "They sit on the headland and watch the mouth when someone's in. Waiting to see." He means it.}
opt.right.say.1 [ee645b] = {at_home() and has(origin_street): “海鸥进去了，”她说，“它们只跟着要淹死的东西进去。”她说得像报个价钱一样平淡。|“海鸥，”他说，“有人在里面的时候，它们就蹲在岬角上盯着洞口。等着看。”他是认真的。}

@thread tide_delve
# en: The tide caves
name [da95a2] = 潮汐洞窟
# en: Under Port Calder's headland, the caves go further in than the tide does.
premise [ac2e4b] = 在考尔德港的岬角底下，那些洞比潮水走得更深。
# en: You read the smugglers' tide ladder in the caves, and know their run past the easy ground.
journal.1 [8d60ce] = 你在洞里读懂了走私者的潮梯，知道了他们绕过好走地段的路。
# en: A culvert from the smugglers' galleries climbs to a grating under the bonded warehouses.
journal.2 [3ee66b] = 走私者坑道里有条涵洞，一直爬到保税仓库底下的一块铁栅。
# en: The conger in the sump gave way to you.
journal.3 [288013] = 水坑里的康吉鳗给你让了路。
# en: At the far end of the caves you stood in the sea's door.
journal.4 [875a94] = 在洞窟的最深处，你站在了海之门里。

@event tide1_drowned_stair
# en: The Drowned Stair
title [07f73e] = 淹没的阶梯
# en: {seen(tide1_drowned_stair) > 1: The drowned stair again. The sea has left a new skin of weed on every step.|Past the mouth the steps go on down, cut into the rock in a tight turn, every one dipped in the middle and slick with weed. At the bottom, water is moving in the dark.}
text [b116a1] = {seen(tide1_drowned_stair) > 1: 又是那道淹没的阶梯。海在每一级上都留下了一层新的海草。|过了洞口，台阶继续往下，在岩石里凿成一道急转的螺旋，每一级中间都凹下去，滑溜溜地长着海草。底下的黑暗里，水在流动。}
# en: Narrow steps cut into wet rock, spiralling down inside a sea cave, slick with green weed, sea water moving at the bottom, a student edging down with a lantern.
scene [93552c] = 湿岩里凿出的窄台阶在海蚀洞里盘旋而下，滑溜溜地长着绿海草，底下海水在流动，一个学生提着灯一点点往下挪。
# en: Turn back here
opt.left.label [3fbec1] = 到这儿就回头
# en: {seen(tide1_drowned_stair) > 1: You decide the stair has made its point, and climb back to the sun.|You go back up into the daylight, one careful step at a time.}
opt.left.say.1 [1e3c19] = {seen(tide1_drowned_stair) > 1: 你认定这台阶已经把话说清楚了，爬回了太阳底下。|你一步一步小心地爬回天光里。}
# en: Climb down
opt.right.label [095c66] = 爬下去
# en: {seen(tide1_drowned_stair) > 1: You take the stair at a crouch and land in ankle-deep water, cold enough to make you gasp, but upright.|You go down sideways like a crab, a hand on the wall, and reach the bottom with all your bones. Somebody has carved a hand on the last step, pointing on.}
opt.right.say.1 [1f2d37] = {seen(tide1_drowned_stair) > 1: 你弓着身子走完台阶，落进齐脚踝深的水里，冷得你倒抽一口气，但人是站着的。|你像螃蟹一样侧着身子往下，一只手扶着墙，骨头一根不少地到了底。有人在最后一级台阶上刻了一只手，指着前方。}
# en: {seen(tide1_drowned_stair) > 1: A step crumbles. You hit the water at the bottom with a noise the whole cave repeats.|Your heel finds the weed. You go down the rest of the stair on your back, faster than any smuggler ever did.}
opt.right.say.2 [70f036] = {seen(tide1_drowned_stair) > 1: 一级台阶塌了。你掉进底下的水里，那声响整个洞都学了一遍。|你的脚跟踩上了海草。你仰面滑完了剩下的台阶，比哪个走私者下得都快。}

@event tide1_gull_cave
# en: The Gull Cave
title [7b3851] = 海鸥洞
# en: {seen(tide1_gull_cave) > 1: The gull cave. They remember you. You can tell.|The passage runs through a high cave, white to the roof, and every ledge in it has a gull on it, and every gull has an opinion. The way on is through the middle of them.}
text [fbfc33] = {seen(tide1_gull_cave) > 1: 海鸥洞。它们记得你。你看得出来。|通道穿过一个高高的洞，一直白到洞顶，每块岩架上都有一只海鸥，每只海鸥都有自己的看法。往前的路就从它们中间穿过去。}
# en: A high sea cave full of shrieking gulls on white-streaked ledges, daylight through a crack in the roof, a student running through with an arm over their head.
scene [24834a] = 一个高高的海蚀洞，满是白色条痕的岩架上挤着尖叫的海鸥，天光从洞顶的裂缝漏下来，一个学生用胳膊护着头跑过去。
# en: Back out quietly
opt.left.label [fd6c99] = 悄悄退出去
# en: {seen(tide1_gull_cave) > 1: You leave the gulls their cave. One follows you to the mouth to make sure.|You back out under a hail of remarks and go home the way you came.}
opt.left.say.1 [eb1eb5] = {seen(tide1_gull_cave) > 1: 你把洞留给海鸥。有一只一直跟你到洞口，确认你走了。|你顶着一阵冷嘲热讽退出去，原路回家。}
# en: Run through them
opt.right.label [920f9b] = 从它们中间冲过去
# en: {seen(tide1_gull_cave) > 1: You run with your collar up and your head down. They aim well, and often.|You run through with your arm over your head. The gulls mob you the whole way, beak and wing and worse, and you come out the far side pecked and plastered.}
opt.right.say.1 [35cc5e] = {seen(tide1_gull_cave) > 1: 你竖起衣领、低着头跑。它们瞄得很准，而且很勤。|你用胳膊护着头冲过去。海鸥一路围攻你，嘴、翅膀，还有更糟的，你从另一头出来时被啄得满身狼藉。}
# en: Ward your head and walk
opt.up.label [2b0492] = 罩住头走过去
# en: {seen(tide1_gull_cave) > 1: Ward up, you walk through. Everything the gulls contribute runs off the shell like rain off a window.|You raise a pale shell over your head and walk through at a stroll. Everything they throw slides off it. The gulls are outraged.}
opt.up.say.1 [b1974d] = {seen(tide1_gull_cave) > 1: 护盾一撑，你走了过去。海鸥贡献的一切都从壳上流下去，像雨水流下窗玻璃。|你在头顶撑起一层淡淡的壳，慢悠悠地走过去。它们扔下来的东西全滑开了。海鸥们气坏了。}

@event tide1_tide_ladder
# en: The Tide Ladder
title [e3aedc] = 潮梯
# en: {seen(tide1_tide_ladder) > 1: The tide ladder again, half under water today. The notches above the waterline point to a gallery you've never taken.|On the passage wall someone has cut a ladder of notches, one above another like the rungs of a ladder, each with a mark cut beside it, a hook to the left or a hook to the right: at this height of water, this gallery. The smugglers kept their tide-table where they needed it.}
text [cc675a] = {seen(tide1_tide_ladder) > 1: 又是潮梯，今天一半在水下。水线以上的刻痕指向一条你从没走过的坑道。|通道的墙上有人刻了一架刻痕梯子，一道叠一道，像梯子的横档，每道旁边刻着一个记号，钩向左或者钩向右：水到这个高度，就走这条坑道。走私者把潮汐表刻在了用得着的地方。}
# en: The wall of a sea cave scored with a tall ladder of old notches, a hooked mark beside each, a high-water line of weed across them, a student holding a lantern up to read them.
scene [617f1b] = 海蚀洞的墙上刻着一长排古老的刻痕，每道旁边有个钩形记号，一道海草的高水线横过它们，一个学生举着灯在看。
# en: Leave it and turn back
opt.left.label [d1faaa] = 不管它，回头
# en: {seen(tide1_tide_ladder) > 1: You turn back. Every hook on the wall seems to point the other way.|You leave the notches to the next smuggler and head back to the light.}
opt.left.say.1 [979e08] = {seen(tide1_tide_ladder) > 1: 你往回走。墙上每个钩好像都指着另一边。|你把这些刻痕留给下一个走私者，往有光的地方回去。}
# en: Work out the ladder
opt.right.label [8ffaa1] = 弄懂这道潮梯
# en: {seen(tide1_tide_ladder) > 1: You read the ladder from the bottom up, the way it was cut, and all at once you know the way the smugglers walked.|It takes an hour and most of your patience, but it comes clear: at this water, the left-hand gallery, then the dry crawl. It's the smugglers' run, and it goes straight past the easy caves.}
opt.right.say.1 [473ce3] = {seen(tide1_tide_ladder) > 1: 你照着刻的顺序从下往上读，忽然就知道了走私者当年走的路。|花了一个钟头，耗掉你大半的耐心，但终于看明白了：这个水位，走左手那条坑道，然后是那段干的爬道。这是走私者的路，径直越过那些好走的洞。}
# en: {seen(tide1_tide_ladder) > 1: You squint at the notches until they swim. It means something, to someone. Not to you, not today.|The hooks contradict each other and half the notches are worn smooth. You go on the slow way with a headache.}
opt.right.say.2 [07b5c4] = {seen(tide1_tide_ladder) > 1: 你眯着眼看那些刻痕，直到它们开始游动。这对某个人有意义。不是对你，不是今天。|那些钩互相矛盾，一半的刻痕都磨平了。你头疼地走了那条慢路。}

@event tide1_wreck_ribs
# en: Ship's Ribs
title [605075] = 船肋
# en: {seen(tide1_wreck_ribs) > 1: The wreck in the passage, a little more broken than last time. The sea is taking it back plank by plank.|Jammed across the passage, where some great sea must have thrown it, are the ribs of a boat: black oak, green copper nails, the stump of a mast. Whoever was in it isn't.}
text [e6d0ce] = {seen(tide1_wreck_ribs) > 1: 通道里的残骸，比上次又碎了一些。海正一块板一块板地把它收回去。|横卡在通道里的，是一条船的肋骨，想必是哪次大浪扔进来的：黑橡木，绿铜钉，半截桅杆。船上的人不在了。}
# en: The black curved ribs of an old wooden boat jammed between rocks deep in a sea cave, green copper nails in the timbers, a student working one loose with a knife.
scene [896701] = 一条旧木船弯曲的黑色肋骨卡在海蚀洞深处的岩石之间，木头上钉着绿铜钉，一个学生用刀撬着其中一根。
# en: Leave it be and turn back
opt.left.label [9d37d9] = 别动它，回头
# en: {seen(tide1_wreck_ribs) > 1: You turn back. Behind you the old timbers creak as the water lifts them.|You leave the wreck to the sea and go back toward the light.}
opt.left.say.1 [6a23a5] = {seen(tide1_wreck_ribs) > 1: 你往回走。身后，海水抬起旧木头，嘎吱作响。|你把残骸留给海，往有光的地方回去。}
# en: Strip the copper
opt.right.label [f425b3] = 把铜扒下来
# en: {seen(tide1_wreck_ribs) > 1: You prise a brass rowlock off the gunwale and gash your palm doing it. The wreck groans as you climb over it.|You work the green nails out of the oak with your knife and a stone, and take the skin off two knuckles. Copper's copper, the dealers say.}
opt.right.say.1 [b62ae8] = {seen(tide1_wreck_ribs) > 1: 你从船舷上撬下一个黄铜桨架，手掌被划了个口子。你从它上面爬过时，残骸呻吟了一声。|你用刀和一块石头把绿铜钉从橡木里撬出来，两个指关节蹭掉了皮。铜就是铜，旧货商们都这么说。}

@event tide1_blowhole
# en: The Blowhole
title [8fd582] = 喷水洞
# en: {&A long passage, lit from above: a hole in the roof lets down a shaft of daylight, and every wave that comes in somewhere below sends a breath of spray up through it, glittering.|The blowhole passage. The spray hangs in the light like dust.|Daylight from the roof, and voices somewhere ahead that are seals, or sound like seals.} For a while the caves are only caves.
text [7e2d87] = {&一条长长的通道，光从上面来：洞顶一个窟窿漏下一道天光，下面某处每涌进一个浪，就有一股水雾从那里升上来，闪闪发亮。|喷水洞的通道。水雾悬在光里，像灰尘。|洞顶漏下天光，前方某处传来声音，是海豹，或者听着像海豹。} 有那么一会儿，这些洞只是洞。
# en: A long sea cave passage lit by a shaft of daylight falling through a hole in the roof, spray drifting up through the light, a student walking through it.
scene [5e5909] = 一条长长的海蚀洞通道，一道天光从洞顶的窟窿落下，水雾穿过光柱飘上去，一个学生从中走过。
# en: Turn back while it's easy
opt.left.label [d572f3] = 趁好走赶紧回头
# en: {&You turn round while the going is good, and are out on the rocks before the light changes.|You turn back under the blowhole, with dry feet and a clear head.|You turn back. The seal voices follow you a while, then stop.}
opt.left.say.1 [0b4429] = {&你趁着好走转身，光线还没变就已经回到外面的礁石上了。|你在喷水洞下回头，脚是干的，脑子是清的。|你往回走。海豹的声音跟了你一阵，然后停了。}
# en: Go on
opt.right.label [8d20dc] = 继续走
# en: {&You walk on through the spray, and the passage climbs into the dark.|You go on, out past where the daylight reaches.|You go on toward the voices. Somewhere past the blowhole, they stop.}
opt.right.say.1 [e4491e] = {&你穿过水雾往前走，通道往上爬进黑暗里。|你继续往前，走出天光照得到的地方。|你朝那些声音走去。过了喷水洞某处，它们停了。}

@event tide2_lookout
# en: The Lookout
title [4c8d61] = 望风的人
# en: {seen(tide2_lookout) > 1: The lookout again, or another one. He knows what you are now, and doesn't bother asking.|Up here, above the tide, the galleries are dry, and somebody uses them: fresh rope, a stack of casks, a pipe still warm on a ledge. And a lookout, coming round the corner with a shuttered lantern, who sees you and sets it down very carefully, to free his wand hand.}
text [aca626] = {seen(tide2_lookout) > 1: 又是那个望风的，或者另一个。他现在知道你是什么人了，懒得再问。|到了这上面，潮水之上，坑道是干的，而且有人在用：新绳子，一摞木桶，岩架上一只烟斗还是温的。还有一个望风的，提着一盏遮光灯从拐角转过来，看见你，非常小心地把灯放下，好腾出拿魔杖的手。}
# en: A rough man with a shuttered lantern and a cheap wand standing in a dry rock gallery stacked with casks inside a sea cave, glaring at a student who has just come round the corner.
scene [82dc5d] = 海蚀洞里一条堆满木桶的干燥岩石坑道，一个提着遮光灯、拿着廉价魔杖的粗汉瞪着刚从拐角转过来的学生。
# en: Back off the way you came
opt.left.label [7a3152] = 原路退回去
# en: {seen(tide2_lookout) > 1: You go back the way you came. He watches you to the end of the gallery, wand out.|You back away round the corner with your hands up, and he lets you, which is the best offer you'll get today.}
opt.left.say.1 [127d49] = {seen(tide2_lookout) > 1: 你原路回去。他举着魔杖看着你一直走到坑道尽头。|你举着双手退回拐角，他也放你走了，今天你能得到的最好待遇就是这个。}
# en: Fight your way past
opt.right.label [57378d] = 打过去
# en: He fights dirty, with the forbidden kind of magic.
opt.right.hint [145433] = 他打得下作，用的是禁术那一类魔法。
# en: {seen(tide2_lookout) > 1: You leave him sitting against the wall holding his head. On the ledge behind him, under the dust, someone long gone left a brass lantern. You take it.|He goes down among his own casks, and stays down. In the scuffle a brass spyglass has rolled out from under the casks, dusty, nobody's for years. It's going to the dealer on the quay.}
opt.right.say.1 [0c06ee] = {seen(tide2_lookout) > 1: 你留他抱着头靠墙坐着。他身后的岩架上，积灰底下，有个早已不在的人留下了一盏黄铜灯。你拿走了。|他倒在自己的木桶之间，起不来了。扭打中，一具黄铜望远镜从木桶底下滚了出来，落满了灰，多年没有主人。它要去码头上的旧货商那儿了。}
# en: {seen(tide2_lookout) > 1: Something nasty and quick comes off his wand and you go down, and he rolls you back down the gallery like a cask, into the sea.|He's had more fights in the dark than you've had lessons. You come to at the bottom of the gallery, by the water, with a lump and no lantern.}
opt.right.say.2 [09db9b] = {seen(tide2_lookout) > 1: 他的魔杖里射出一道又阴又快的东西，你倒了下去，他把你像推木桶一样推下坑道，推进海里。|他在黑暗里打过的架比你上过的课还多。你醒过来时躺在坑道底下的水边，头上一个包，灯也没了。}
# en: Pass for a new hand
opt.up.label [ea491b] = 冒充新来的帮手
# en: {seen(tide2_lookout) > 1: You smile, and he decides he likes you. He even tells you to mind the step.|You put on a little more charm than you have and tell him you're the new hand. He looks you up and down, grunts, and waves you on past the casks. He won't remember why.}
opt.up.say.1 [556f3a] = {seen(tide2_lookout) > 1: 你一笑，他就决定喜欢你了。他甚至提醒你小心台阶。|你装出比实际多一点的魅力，告诉他你是新来的帮手。他上下打量你，哼了一声，挥手让你从木桶边过去。他不会记得为什么。}

@event tide2_casks
# en: The Cask Gallery
title [d865f8] = 木桶坑道
# en: {seen(tide2_casks) > 1: The cask gallery again. The stacks have changed since last time: the trade goes on.|A long dry gallery, stacked to the roof: casks, oilcloth bales, tea chests with the customs seals neatly cut. Somebody's whole business, waiting for a dark night. Nobody's minding it this minute.}
text [8be93f] = {seen(tide2_casks) > 1: 又是木桶坑道。货堆和上次不一样了：生意照做。|一条长长的干坑道，一直堆到顶：木桶、油布包、茶叶箱，海关的封条被整整齐齐地割开了。某个人的全部家当，等着一个漆黑的夜晚。这会儿没人看着。}
# en: A long dry rock gallery inside sea caves stacked with barrels, oilcloth bales and tea chests, ropes and a block-and-tackle, a student with a lantern looking at a cut customs seal.
scene [b76c91] = 海蚀洞里一条长长的干燥岩石坑道，堆着木桶、油布包和茶叶箱，有绳子和滑车，一个提灯的学生看着一张被割开的海关封条。
# en: Leave it and turn back
opt.left.label [d1faaa] = 不管它，回头
# en: {seen(tide2_casks) > 1: You leave the stacks to their owners and head back to the light.|You touch nothing and go back the way you came, which is what smugglers like best in a visitor.}
opt.left.say.1 [0b288e] = {seen(tide2_casks) > 1: 你把货堆留给它们的主人，往有光的地方回去。|你什么也没碰，原路回去，走私者最喜欢这样的客人。}
# en: Help yourself and go on
opt.right.label [4a05b5] = 顺手拿点，继续走
# en: {seen(tide2_casks) > 1: You take your pick of the new stacks: tea, and a case of something from over the sea. It's stealing, and you know it, and you take it anyway.|You fill your bag from a tea chest and a case of something in bottles. It's stealing from thieves, but it's stealing, and you go on quickly.}
opt.right.say.1 [02c0e3] = {seen(tide2_casks) > 1: 你在新的货堆里挑了挑：茶叶，还有一箱从海那边来的什么东西。这是偷，你心里清楚，还是拿了。|你从一个茶叶箱和一箱瓶装货里装满了袋子。偷贼也是偷，你赶紧往前走。}

@event tide2_culvert
# en: The Culvert
title [d9d62f] = 涵洞
# en: {seen(tide2_culvert) > 1: The culvert again, and the grating at the top, and through it the warehouse floor: crates stencilled with the customs crown, a watchman's boots going by on his round.|Off the gallery a brick culvert climbs steeply, much newer than the caves, built to drain something. At the top there's an iron grating, and through the bars, lamplight, crates stencilled with the customs crown, and a watchman's boots going by. The bonded warehouses, from underneath.}
text [10b220] = {seen(tide2_culvert) > 1: 又是那条涵洞，顶上的铁栅，透过它是仓库的地面：印着海关王冠的板条箱，一个看守的靴子在巡夜路上走过。|坑道边有一条砖砌的涵洞陡直地往上爬，比那些洞新得多，是为了排什么水修的。顶上是一块铁栅，透过栅栏能看见灯光、印着海关王冠的板条箱，还有一个看守的靴子走过。这是保税仓库，从底下看。}
# en: A brick-lined culvert climbing steeply from a sea cave gallery up to an iron grating, lamplight and stencilled crates visible through the bars above, a student lying in the culvert looking up.
scene [1f6c91] = 一条砖砌涵洞从海蚀洞坑道陡直地爬到一块铁栅，透过栅栏能看见上面的灯光和印着字的板条箱，一个学生躺在涵洞里往上看。
# en: Leave it and turn back
opt.left.label [d1faaa] = 不管它，回头
# en: {seen(tide2_culvert) > 1: You leave the warehouse to its watchman and go back down to the sea.|You climb back down very quietly and go home with the grating in your head.}
opt.left.say.1 [d8b906] = {seen(tide2_culvert) > 1: 你把仓库留给它的看守，回到海那边去。|你轻手轻脚地爬下去，回家时脑子里全是那块铁栅。}
# en: Lie under it and watch
opt.right.label [4205b2] = 躺在底下看着
# en: {flag(bonded_round_counted): You count the watchman's round again from under the grating, cramped and cold: the same slow circuit, the same long gap at the far end. Then you climb down and go on.|You lie in the culvert under the grating, cramped and cold, and count the watchman's round: a slow circuit, then a long gap at the far end of the floor. Nobody looks down. Then you climb back and go on.}
opt.right.say.1 [f1c20f] = {flag(bonded_round_counted): 你又在铁栅底下数了一遍看守的巡夜，蜷着身子，冷得发僵：还是那慢悠悠的一圈，远端还是那段长长的空当。然后你爬下来继续走。|你躺在铁栅下的涵洞里，蜷着身子，冷得发僵，数着看守的巡夜：慢悠悠的一圈，然后在地面远端有一段长长的空当。没人往下看。然后你爬回去，继续走。}

@event tide2_turning
# en: The Turn of the Tide
title [b529b9] = 潮水回头
# en: {seen(tide2_turning) > 1: The tide again, early again. You know the sound now, and so do your legs.|From behind you comes a sound like a long breath drawn in. The tide has turned, early, and the water is coming up the gallery faster than walking pace. Ahead, the gallery climbs. Behind is the way out, and it's filling.}
text [1e02c8] = {seen(tide2_turning) > 1: 又是潮水，又提前了。你现在认得这声音了，你的腿也认得。|身后传来一声长长的吸气似的声响。潮水回头了，提前了，水正顺着坑道往上涌，比走路还快。前面，坑道往上爬。后面是出路，正在灌满。}
# en: Sea water surging up a narrow rock gallery in a sea cave, white foam in lantern light, a student running uphill ahead of it.
scene [202bbb] = 海水顺着海蚀洞里一条窄窄的岩石坑道往上涌，灯光里白沫翻滚，一个学生在前面往坡上跑。
# en: Run back out while you can
opt.left.label [dd7135] = 趁还来得及跑出去
# en: {seen(tide2_turning) > 1: You splash out the way you came, against the sea, and fall out of the mouth onto the rocks soaked to the neck.|You run back down into the rising water and fight it to the mouth, waist-deep at the end, coughing salt.}
opt.left.say.1 [b95178] = {seen(tide2_turning) > 1: 你逆着海水原路蹚出去，从洞口栽到外面的礁石上，水一直湿到脖子。|你跑回上涨的水里，一路拼到洞口，最后水齐了腰，咳出一嘴咸水。}
# en: Race it uphill
opt.right.label [92737d] = 和它赛跑上坡
# en: {seen(tide2_turning) > 1: You beat it by a step and sit on the dry rock above, laughing at it.|You go up the gallery at a run with the sea at your heels and scramble onto a dry ledge as it slaps the rock below you. It sulks there a while, then sinks back.}
opt.right.say.1 [4c8c9c] = {seen(tide2_turning) > 1: 你只比它快了一步，坐在上面干燥的岩石上冲它笑。|你在海水紧追下一路跑上坑道，爬上一块干岩架时，海正拍在你脚下的岩石上。它在那里赌了会儿气，又退了下去。}
# en: {seen(tide2_turning) > 1: The water's quicker. You end up wrapped round a rock with the sea pulling at your bag.|It catches you halfway, knocks your feet from under you, and you go tumbling back down the gallery in a smother of foam.}
opt.right.say.2 [6e8405] = {seen(tide2_turning) > 1: 水更快。你最后抱住了一块石头，海在扯你的袋子。|它在半路追上你，把你的脚扫倒，你裹在一团白沫里翻滚着跌回坑道下面。}
# en: Let the wind take you
opt.up.label [676c23] = 让风推着你
# en: {seen(tide2_turning) > 1: You call the wind and run. The sea arrives at the top to find you sitting there, dry.|A wind gets behind you and you go up the gallery like a cork out of a bottle, well ahead of the sea.}
opt.up.say.1 [495c1d] = {seen(tide2_turning) > 1: 你唤来风就跑。海到了坡顶，发现你已经干干地坐在那儿了。|一阵风从背后推着你，你像瓶塞一样冲上坑道，把海远远甩在后面。}

@event tide2_parlour
# en: The Smugglers' Parlour
title [463cdf] = 走私者的客厅
# en: {seen(tide2_parlour) > 1: The smugglers' parlour. Somebody has played a game of fox-and-geese since you were here, and the geese won.|Off the gallery there's a room: a chamber in the rock fitted out like a parlour, with benches, a hearth and a kettle hook, a fox-and-geese board cut into the table, and shelves of dusty bottles. A chimney goes up into the headland. Somebody lived down here, between tides.}
text [0c94ca] = {seen(tide2_parlour) > 1: 走私者的客厅。你上次来过之后，有人在这里下过一盘狐狸与鹅，鹅赢了。|坑道边有个房间：岩石里的一间石室布置得像客厅，有长凳、壁炉和挂水壶的钩子，桌上刻着一块狐狸与鹅的棋盘，架子上摆着落满灰的瓶子。一根烟囱通到岬角上面。曾经有人住在这下面，在两次潮水之间。}
# en: A small rock chamber in a sea cave fitted out as a room: benches, a rough table with a game board cut into it, a hearth with a kettle hook, shelves of old bottles, a student with a lantern looking round.
scene [a6beff] = 海蚀洞里一间布置成房间的小石室：长凳，一张刻着棋盘的粗桌，挂着水壶钩的壁炉，摆着旧瓶子的架子，一个提灯的学生四下张望。
# en: Leave it and turn back
opt.left.label [d1faaa] = 不管它，回头
# en: {seen(tide2_parlour) > 1: You turn back. The parlour's chimney sighs as you go.|You leave the parlour as you found it and go back toward the sea.}
opt.left.say.1 [28863c] = {seen(tide2_parlour) > 1: 你往回走。你走的时候，客厅的烟囱叹了口气。|你把客厅留成原样，回到海那边去。}
# en: Search the shelves
opt.right.label [e719ca] = 搜搜架子
# en: {seen(tide2_parlour) > 1: You go along the shelves and find a tin of old tobacco and a brass tinder-box, and splinters in both hands from the rotten wood.|You go along the shelves, and one comes down on your head, bottles and all. Two are still whole, and still full. You take them and go on, rubbing your skull.}
opt.right.say.1 [174682] = {seen(tide2_parlour) > 1: 你沿着架子搜，找到一罐陈烟草和一个黄铜火绒盒，两只手都扎满了朽木刺。|你沿着架子搜，一块架板连瓶子一起砸在你头上。有两瓶还是完好的，还是满的。你揉着脑袋，拿上它们继续走。}

@event tide3_conger
# en: The Conger
title [a67cb6] = 康吉鳗
# en: {seen(tide3_conger) > 1: The sump, and the conger in it. It comes up to look at you, slow and grey, and remembers.|The only way on is a ledge round a black sump pool, and something lives in the pool. A grey head comes up out of it, then more of it, and more, thick as a man's leg, jaws working. A conger, longer than a rowing boat, between you and the rest of the caves.}
text [c50680] = {seen(tide3_conger) > 1: 水坑，还有坑里的康吉鳗。它浮上来看你，缓慢、灰色，它记得。|往前只有一条岩架绕过一个黑水坑，坑里住着东西。一个灰色的头从水里冒出来，接着是更多，再更多，有人的腿那么粗，嘴巴一张一合。一条康吉鳗，比划艇还长，挡在你和其余的洞之间。}
# en: An enormous grey conger eel, thick as a man's leg, rearing out of a black pool in a sea cave with its jaws open, a student on the narrow rock ledge beside the pool.
scene [cba70f] = 一条巨大的灰色康吉鳗，有人的腿那么粗，张着嘴从海蚀洞的黑水坑里昂起身子，一个学生站在水坑边窄窄的岩架上。
# en: Back off the ledge
opt.left.label [7dd031] = 退下岩架
# en: {seen(tide3_conger) > 1: You leave the conger its pool. All the way out you can feel the water behind you, deciding.|You back off the ledge very slowly. The conger watches you all the way, then sinks.}
opt.left.say.1 [688ed7] = {seen(tide3_conger) > 1: 你把水坑留给康吉鳗。一路出去，你都能感觉到身后的水在掂量。|你非常缓慢地退下岩架。康吉鳗一直盯着你，然后沉了下去。}
# en: Fight it off the ledge
opt.right.label [88a255] = 把它打下岩架
# en: It strikes from its hole and drags back into it: hit it when it shows.
opt.right.hint [68b952] = 它从洞里扑出来，又缩回去：趁它露头时打。
# en: {seen(tide3_conger) > 1: You drive it down into the black water and the pool goes still. Crossing the ledge with your back to the wall, you pick up a tooth it left on the rock, as long as your finger.|It slides back into its hole and stays there, sulking, one eye on you. On the ledge where it struck there's a tooth as long as your finger. You take it.}
opt.right.say.1 [eaa276] = {seen(tide3_conger) > 1: 你把它逼进黑水里，水坑平静下来。你背贴着墙走过岩架，捡起它留在石头上的一颗牙，有你的手指那么长。|它滑回洞里不出来了，生着闷气，一只眼睛盯着你。它扑过的岩架上留下一颗牙，有你的手指那么长。你拿走了。}
# en: {seen(tide3_conger) > 1: It catches your sleeve and pulls, and you leave the sleeve with it, and a good deal of skin.|It comes up out of the pool faster than anything that size should, and you go into the water. You get out. You don't remember how.}
opt.right.say.2 [e65805] = {seen(tide3_conger) > 1: 它咬住你的袖子往下拖，你把袖子留给了它，还有好大一块皮。|它从水坑里窜出来，快得不像那么大的东西，你掉进了水里。你爬了出来。不记得是怎么爬出来的。}
# en: Seal it in its hole
opt.up.label [d22a80] = 把它封在洞里
# en: {seen(tide3_conger) > 1: You seal its hole with a word. Something thumps against the seal from below, hard, twice, and then you're past.|You close the mouth of its hole with a word, long enough to cross. The pool heaves once, twice, and lies still, and you go round the ledge with the conger thumping somewhere under your feet.}
opt.up.say.1 [86694f] = {seen(tide3_conger) > 1: 你念一个词封住它的洞。底下有东西撞在封印上，很重，两下，然后你已经过去了。|你念一个词封住它的洞口，够你过去的工夫。水坑翻腾了一下，两下，然后静了，你绕过岩架，康吉鳗在你脚下某处咚咚地撞。}

@event tide3_glow_pool
# en: The Shining Pool
title [4dd88a] = 发光的水潭
# en: {seen(tide3_glow_pool) > 1: The shining pool again. It flares where your shadow falls on it.|In the dark beyond the sump there's a pool that shines: a soft blue-green light coming up out of the water, brighter where you stir it, as if the pool were full of sparks that mind being touched.}
text [8c22dd] = {seen(tide3_glow_pool) > 1: 又是那个发光的水潭。你的影子落到哪里，它就在哪里亮起来。|过了水坑的黑暗里有个会发光的潭：柔和的蓝绿色光从水里透上来，你一搅就更亮，好像潭里满是火花，又不喜欢被碰。}
# en: A dark sea cave chamber with a still pool glowing soft blue-green with tiny living lights, a student kneeling at the edge filling a glass phial with glowing water.
scene [4f9ae6] = 海蚀洞里一间黑暗的石室，一潭静水泛着柔和的蓝绿色微光，一个学生跪在潭边，用玻璃小瓶装发光的水。
# en: Leave it shining and turn back
opt.left.label [4656e2] = 让它亮着，回头
# en: {seen(tide3_glow_pool) > 1: You turn back. Behind you the pool settles, and dims, and waits.|You leave the pool to its light. All the way out, the dark seems darker.}
opt.left.say.1 [c1abec] = {seen(tide3_glow_pool) > 1: 你往回走。身后的水潭平静下来，暗了，等着。|你让水潭留着它的光。一路出去，黑暗好像更黑了。}
# en: Fill a phial and go on
opt.right.label [87308b] = 装一瓶，继续走
# en: {seen(tide3_glow_pool) > 1: You fill a phial. The water is so cold your fingers stop working, but the glass in your bag lights your way on.|You fill a phial. The light in it swirls, then settles, still glowing. Your hand, where it touched the water, stings and glows faintly for an hour.}
opt.right.say.1 [a257f3] = {seen(tide3_glow_pool) > 1: 你装了一小瓶。水冷得你手指都不听使唤了，可袋子里那瓶光给你照亮了前路。|你装了一小瓶。里面的光旋了旋，沉下来，还在亮。你碰过水的那只手又刺又疼，微微发了一个钟头的光。}

@event tide3_figurehead
# en: The Figurehead
title [94ca66] = 船首像
# en: {flag(tide_figurehead_stripped): The figurehead looks down the passage at you, her fist empty where the lamp was, as she has done for a hundred years.|{seen(tide3_figurehead) > 1: The figurehead looks down the passage at you, lamp up, as she has done for a hundred years.|High in the rock, where no ship could have put her, is a figurehead: a carved woman holding up a lamp, her paint long gone and her gilt flaking, looking straight down the passage at whoever comes. The lamp in her fist is real brass.}}
text [000194] = {flag(tide_figurehead_stripped): 船首像顺着通道低头看你，她的拳头空着，那里曾经是灯，她这样看了一百年了。|{seen(tide3_figurehead) > 1: 船首像举着灯，顺着通道低头看你，她这样看了一百年了。|高高的岩石里，没有哪条船能把她放到那里，有一尊船首像：一个举着灯的木雕女人，漆早没了，镀金一片片剥落，径直望着通道里来的每一个人。她拳头里的灯是真黄铜的。}}
# en: A carved wooden ship's figurehead of a woman holding up a brass lamp, her paint gone and her gilt flaking, wedged high in the rock of a sea cave, a student looking up at her with a lantern.
scene [25d947] = 一尊举着黄铜灯的木雕女人船首像，漆已脱落、镀金剥落，卡在海蚀洞高处的岩石里，一个提灯的学生抬头看她。
# en: Leave her be and turn back
opt.left.label [4fb8b3] = 别打扰她，回头
# en: {seen(tide3_figurehead) > 1: You turn back. Her eyes are only paint. You check twice.|You leave her to her watch and go back the way you came. You don't look round.}
opt.left.say.1 [caa89c] = {seen(tide3_figurehead) > 1: 你往回走。她的眼睛只是漆。你看了两遍。|你让她继续守着，原路回去。你没有回头。}
# en: Climb up and strip her brass
opt.right.label [04d212] = 爬上去扒她的黄铜
# en: {flag(tide_figurehead_stripped): You climb her and scrape away what gilt the sea has left her, grazing both hands. She doesn't seem to mind, which is somehow worse.|You climb her and work the lamp out of her wooden fist, splinters in both palms. It comes away with a crack. Walking on, you keep feeling her looking at the back of your neck.}
opt.right.say.1 [f63c62] = {flag(tide_figurehead_stripped): 你爬上她，刮下海给她留下的那点镀金，两只手都蹭破了。她好像并不在意，这反倒更糟。|你爬上她，把灯从她的木拳里撬出来，两只手掌扎满了木刺。灯咔嚓一声下来了。继续往前走时，你一直觉得她在盯着你的后颈。}
# en: Mend her
opt.up.label [c92dae] = 修补她
# en: You knit the cracks in her face and arm with Mend, and a little of the paint comes back, where it can. You think she's smiling. You're probably wrong, but you walk on lighter.
opt.up.say.1 [567542] = 你用修补术弥合她脸上和胳膊上的裂缝，漆也回来了一点，能回来的地方。你觉得她在笑。你多半想错了，但你走得轻松了些。

@event tide3_sea_hall
# en: The Sea's Hall
title [2fb1cc] = 海之厅
# en: {seen(tide3_sea_hall) > 1: The great hall of the sea, booming. The ledge is wetter than last time.|The passage opens into a cave as big as the cathedral, and louder: every wave that comes in from somewhere ahead goes off in it like a cannon. The only way across is a ledge along the wall, a foot wide and wet with spray.}
text [b1ada4] = {seen(tide3_sea_hall) > 1: 海的大厅，轰鸣不止。岩架比上次更湿了。|通道通进一个和大教堂一样大的洞，还要更响：前方某处涌进来的每个浪，在里面都像开炮。过去的唯一办法是沿墙的一条岩架，一尺宽，被浪沫打得湿透。}
# en: An enormous sea cave as tall as a cathedral, waves booming in from a distant opening, a narrow wet ledge along one wall, a tiny student with a lantern edging along it.
scene [5710eb] = 一个和大教堂一样高的巨大海蚀洞，浪从远处的开口轰隆隆涌进来，一面墙上有条窄窄的湿岩架，一个提灯的小小学生正贴着它挪过去。
# en: Turn back
opt.left.label [2f9f2d] = 回头
# en: {seen(tide3_sea_hall) > 1: You go back. The hall doesn't notice. It's busy with the sea.|You turn back with the boom of the hall in your chest, and it follows you most of the way out.}
opt.left.say.1 [11ac55] = {seen(tide3_sea_hall) > 1: 你回去了。大厅没注意到。它忙着和海打交道。|你带着胸口里大厅的轰鸣回头，那声音跟了你大半路。}
# en: Edge along the ledge
opt.right.label [fbdc9b] = 贴着岩架挪过去
# en: {seen(tide3_sea_hall) > 1: You cross timing the swell, a step between each wave. The spray soaks you, and doesn't stop you.|You go along the ledge with your face to the rock, counting the waves, moving between them. At the far end you sit down hard and laugh with your whole body.}
opt.right.say.1 [d3168e] = {seen(tide3_sea_hall) > 1: 你踩着浪涌的节奏过去，两个浪之间走一步。浪沫把你淋透，却拦不住你。|你脸贴着岩石沿岩架走，数着浪，在浪与浪之间移动。到了那头，你一屁股坐下，笑得全身发抖。}
# en: {seen(tide3_sea_hall) > 1: You lose the count. A big one finds you halfway, and the hall's floor is a long way down, and wet.|A wave bigger than the others comes in and takes you off the ledge as easily as a hand wiping a table.}
opt.right.say.2 [e8d381] = {seen(tide3_sea_hall) > 1: 你数乱了。一个大浪在半路找上你，大厅的地面很远，而且是湿的。|一个比别的都大的浪涌进来，把你从岩架上抹下去，像手抹桌子一样轻松。}
# en: Brace against the swell
opt.up.label [e545d5] = 稳住身子顶住浪
# en: {seen(tide3_sea_hall) > 1: You brace and cross. The sea slams into you twice and both times it's the sea that gives.|You plant your feet and hold, and when the waves hit you they land soft. You cross the ledge one braced step at a time, soaked and steady.}
opt.up.say.1 [91e45e] = {seen(tide3_sea_hall) > 1: 你稳住身子过去。海撞了你两次，两次都是海让了步。|你站稳脚跟顶住，浪打在身上都轻了。你一步一稳地走过岩架，浑身湿透，稳稳当当。}

@event tide3_strongbox
# en: The Strongbox
title [92156c] = 保险箱
# en: {seen(tide3_strongbox) > 1: Another strongbox in another pool, or the same one shifted by the sea. The caves keep a lot of somebody's money.|At the bottom of a clear pool, sunk in sand, there's a strongbox, iron-bound, its padlock furred with rust. Somebody hid it where only the lowest water shows it, and never came back.}
text [0a0f2e] = {seen(tide3_strongbox) > 1: 又一个水潭里又一个保险箱，或者是同一个被海挪了地方。这些洞替某个人收着好多钱。|一个清澈的水潭底下，半埋在沙里，有个包铁的保险箱，挂锁锈得长了毛。有人把它藏在只有最低的水位才露出来的地方，再也没回来。}
# en: An iron-bound strongbox half sunk in the sand of a clear rock pool in a sea cave, a rusted padlock on it, a student kneeling at the edge with a knife.
scene [7ae8c9] = 海蚀洞里一个清澈的礁石潭，包铁的保险箱半埋在沙里，挂着生锈的挂锁，一个学生拿着刀跪在潭边。
# en: Leave it and turn back
opt.left.label [d1faaa] = 不管它，回头
# en: {seen(tide3_strongbox) > 1: You turn back. Somebody might still be coming for it. Not you.|You leave the box to whoever's coming back for it, and head for the light.}
opt.left.say.1 [6d72f8] = {seen(tide3_strongbox) > 1: 你往回走。也许还有人会回来取。不是你。|你把箱子留给要回来取它的人，往有光的地方去。}
# en: Prise it open
opt.right.label [db9805] = 撬开它
# en: {seen(tide3_strongbox) > 1: You prise the lid in the freezing water till your hands are raw. Inside, wrapped in oilcloth, some dead smuggler's savings.|You wade in to the waist in ice-cold water and work at the hasp with your knife for half an hour, and it gives, and so does the knife, into your hand. Inside: coin, black with salt, and a lot of it.}
opt.right.say.1 [87bff3] = {seen(tide3_strongbox) > 1: 你在冰冷的水里撬箱盖，直到双手磨破。里面用油布包着，是某个死去的走私者的积蓄。|你蹚进齐腰深的冰水里，用刀撬了半个钟头搭扣，它开了，刀也滑了，扎进你手里。里面是硬币，被盐浸得发黑，好多好多。}
# en: Pick the lock
opt.up.label [924ab6] = 撬开锁
# en: {seen(tide3_strongbox) > 1: You pick it standing knee-deep in the pool, fishing the box up with a hooked pick. Your legs go numb. The bazaar seller would be proud.|Eleven picks, and the eighth does it, after a cold half-hour kneeling in the pool. The rusted padlock opens with a sigh.}
opt.up.say.1 [ea1492] = {seen(tide3_strongbox) > 1: 你站在没膝的潭水里撬锁，用一根钩针把箱子勾上来。腿都冻麻了。集市上那个卖家会为你骄傲的。|十一根撬针，第八根成了，前前后后在潭里冷冷地跪了半个钟头。生锈的挂锁叹了口气，开了。}

@event tide_sea_door
# en: The Sea's Door
title [2a41bf] = 海之门
# en: {flag(tide_sea_door): The sea's door again: the arch, the light, the open sea rolling in under the carved ship. The gulls on the cliff know you now.|At the far end of the caves the dark gives out all at once into light: a great arch in the cliff's foot, open on the sea, the waves rolling in through it green and white. Somebody, a very long time ago, cut a step into each side of it and carved a ship over the top. This is the sea's door, and the caves were its hall.}
text [e27863] = {flag(tide_sea_door): 又是海之门：拱门，天光，大海从雕刻的船下滚滚涌进来。崖上的海鸥现在认得你了。|在洞窟的最深处，黑暗一下子到了头，变成了光：悬崖脚下一道巨大的拱门，对着大海敞开，浪一层层绿白相间地涌进来。很久很久以前，有人在两侧各凿了一级台阶，在顶上刻了一条船。这就是海之门，那些洞是它的厅堂。}
# en: A huge natural rock arch at the far end of a sea cave, opening onto the bright open sea at the foot of tall cliffs, waves rolling in through it, a ship carved over the arch, a student standing small inside it.
scene [536785] = 海蚀洞尽头一道巨大的天然石拱，在高崖脚下对着明亮的大海敞开，浪从中涌进来，拱顶刻着一条船，一个学生小小地站在里面。
# en: Look your fill and go back
opt.left.label [481652] = 看个够，再回去
# en: {flag(tide_sea_door): You stand in the arch till the spray soaks you through, then turn back into the dark for the long way home, cold and happy.|You stand in the door of the sea until you're soaked with spray and the light has filled you up. Then you go back the long way through the dark, cold to the bone and grinning.}
opt.left.say.1 [a766fc] = {flag(tide_sea_door): 你站在拱门里，直到浪沫把你淋透，然后转身走回黑暗，走那条长路回家，冷，但是开心。|你站在海的门里，直到浑身被浪沫湿透，光把你装满。然后你穿过黑暗走那条长路回去，冷到骨头里，咧着嘴笑。}
# en: Swim out round the headland
opt.right.label [71b4b9] = 绕着岬角游出去
# en: The quick way home, if you're strong enough.
opt.right.hint [c2cbf6] = 回家的捷径，如果你够强壮的话。
# en: {flag(tide_sea_door): You swim out through the door and round in the cold green water{tide_haul > 0: , letting the heaviest of your bag go to stay afloat,|} and the anglers on the breakwater cheer you in like an old friend.|You go out through the door with a wave and round the headland in the cold green water{tide_haul > 0: , letting the heaviest of your bag go to the sea to stay afloat,|} and come ashore on the breakwater before a dozen anglers who've heard of swimming the door and never seen it done.}
opt.right.say.1 [562acd] = {flag(tide_sea_door): 你从门里游出去，在冰冷的绿水里绕过去{tide_haul > 0: ，为了浮着，放走了袋子里最重的那件，|}防波堤上的钓鱼人像迎老朋友一样欢呼着把你迎上岸。|你随着一个浪从门里出去，在冰冷的绿水里绕过岬角{tide_haul > 0: ，为了浮着，把袋子里最重的那件交给了海，|}在防波堤上一打钓鱼人面前上了岸，他们都听说过游海之门，却从没见人游成过。}
# en: {flag(tide_sea_door): The sea throws you back into the arch like a cat with a mouse. You go home the long way, dripping and humble.|The sea outside the door is stronger than it looks. It throws you back into the arch twice, and the second time you take the hint and walk home the long way, bruised and dripping.}
opt.right.say.2 [25eb71] = {flag(tide_sea_door): 海像猫戏老鼠一样把你扔回拱门里。你走那条长路回家，滴着水，灰溜溜的。|门外的海比看起来凶。它两次把你扔回拱门里，第二次你识相了，走那条长路回家，浑身青紫，滴着水。}
